# Throwaway scripts run against a live database — seeding a branch, planting a
# sign-in code to drive a flow by hand. They are written next to the workspace
# they import from, which is how one of them got committed by a `git add -A`.
# Named rather than tidied up by hand, because the tidying is the step that
# gets skipped.
probe.mts
plant.mts
seed.mts
reseed.mts
cleanup.mts

